&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A highly experienced professional responsible for the strategic and operational regulatory leadership of the company’s global commercialized products in JP, NA, EEA+ and development stage assets. Responsible for developing and delivering innovative, breakthrough global regulatory strategies that support clinical progression and successful marketing applications and label extensions aligned with the global business strategy. Ensures Global Regulatory Affairs Functional Teams (RAFTs) provide high-quality strategic regulatory input to optimize regulatory outcomes and maximize value across the product lifecycle (development through post marketing).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;For products and territories in scope:&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Lead the Global Regulatory Affairs Development and Product Strategy (DP&amp;amp;S) Sub-function.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Oversee the creation and maintenance of global regulatory strategies, ensuring integration of regional requirements, from product inception to end of lifecycle, to optimise regulatory outcomes and maximise product value.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Accountable for the performance and execution of global RA action plan goals pertaining to D&amp;amp;PS, according to pre-specified KPIs agree with the Global Head of RA.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ensure communication to executive leadership, global cross-functional development, commercial and core strategy teams to allow informed strategic decision making and objectives are met in accordance with regulatory requirements, global business goals, timelines and budget.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Identify and assess regulatory risks. Support development of strategies/ countermeasures to mitigate risks. Escalate critical issues to regulatory and/or executive leadership&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Accountable for the preparation and execution of health authority interactions, briefing materials, responses to questions, and negotiation of regulatory positions.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ensure the effective coordination and oversight of global regulatory applications process (e.g. IND, CTA, BLAs, MAA, NDA, NDS) leading to the timely preparation, review and submission of well written, organized and scientifically valid applications and responses, which meet internal and external global standards.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Keep abreast of competitive intelligence and changes in regulatory requirements and environment and assess impact (when required).&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ensure consistent regulatory standards and compliance across programs&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Manage resource requirements, staff, their development and training within D&amp;amp;PS sub-function&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Provide global Regulatory support to current and future business partners and provide timely and effective support of due diligence activities to meet company goals for in-licensing/ out-licensing.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Manage GRA budget with respect to D&amp;amp;PS team and relevant products&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Member of the GRA leadership team&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Represent GRA leadership in cross-functional/cross-regional meetings&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ensure alignment with Vision 2030, company Core Values, Kabegoe Principles, and the Global Regulatory Affairs Vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Life science qualification with significant experience in pharmaceutical regulatory affairs.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Extensive regulatory affairs experience within the pharmaceutical or biotechnology industry, including leadership in regulatory development and experience in post-approval regulatory activities&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Proven ability to define and execute regulatory strategies that optimize regulatory outcomes and maximize product value in rare diseases&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Direct experience of leading Health Authority interactions and major applications in US, EU or JP&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Track record of successful people leadership&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience operating in multicultural, matrixed environments, influencing without authority and orchestrating cross functional alignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;As this can be a sedentary position the individual needs to be able to withstand long periods of sitting.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to use keyboard, read and focus intently for long periods of time.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Ability to travel (local and international) with overnight stays.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Flexibility of working hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Competencies specific to the role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong leadership and management capability.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strategic mindset and enterprise thinking&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Excellent negotiation and interpersonal skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Integrity and commitment to compliance and quality&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Cultural sensitivity and ability to develop consensus within a multinational organisation&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Maintain a global view as part of the whole regulatory team Kyowa Kirin Core Competencies: Results Orientated, Sense of Urgency and Flawless in Execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated salary for this position will be &lt;strong&gt;$310,000 to $ 425,000.&lt;/strong&gt; The actual salary offered for this role at commencement of employment may vary based on several factors including but not limited to relevant experience, skill set, qualifications, education (including applicable licenses and certifications, job-based knowledge, location, and other business and organizational needs.&lt;/p&gt;
