&lt;h3&gt;Summary of Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Senior Medical Science Liaison (MSL) will help shape how Kyowa Kirin’s Rare Disease Medical Affairs team engages with healthcare professionals, researchers, and investigators across South Central. In this field-based role, you’ll lead scientific exchange, bring insights from the field into medical strategy, and support research and education. You’ll have the opportunity to own your territory plan, lead field medical initiatives, and mentor fellow MSLs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Territory&lt;/strong&gt;: Dallas, TX; Houston, TX; Phoenix, AZ; and surrounding markets. Candidates must live within the assigned territory. Travel is up to 70%.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;1222&quot; data-end=&quot;1225&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1peydm1&quot; data-start=&quot;1227&quot; data-end=&quot;1250&quot;&gt;Essential Functions&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 []&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and execute a strategic territory plan that uses scientific and stakeholder insights to prioritize engagements, address unmet medical needs, and guide field medical activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain trusted scientific relationships with healthcare professionals, key opinion leaders, researchers, and investigators across the territory and, as appropriate, nationally and internationally. Serve as a regional scientific resource by connecting stakeholders with relevant Kyowa Kirin resources and research collaborations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide timely, accurate, balanced, and evidence-based information on disease states, treatment options, emerging clinical evidence, and Kyowa Kirin products. Respond to unsolicited medical information requests in accordance with company policy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gather and analyze field insights on unmet medical needs, treatment trends, and the competitive landscape. Translate those insights into recommendations for Medical Affairs strategy, scientific education, and evidence generation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and deliver scientific presentations, educational programs, and resources for external stakeholders and internal teams. Support speaker identification, development, and training as appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the scientific liaison for unsolicited investigator-initiated study proposals and ongoing studies. Partner with Clinical Operations and other internal teams to support company-sponsored studies as appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead field medical activities and provide scientific support at regional, national, and international congresses, advisory boards, investigator meetings, and other scientific forums.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead or contribute to Medical Affairs initiatives, strategic planning, and cross-functional projects. Mentor fellow MSLs by sharing scientific expertise, field insights, and best practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maintain expertise through regular review of clinical literature, treatment guidelines, and emerging evidence. Communicate relevant product safety information in accordance with applicable requirements and company policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate across functions while maintaining appropriate boundaries between scientific and commercial activities. Participate in medical and promotional review as required, and conduct all activities in accordance with applicable laws, regulations, industry codes, and company policies, including pharmacovigilance and privacy requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;4051&quot; data-end=&quot;4054&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;g9ewcs&quot; data-start=&quot;4056&quot; data-end=&quot;4069&quot;&gt;Education&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Advanced clinical or scientific degree or healthcare professional credential required (e.g., MD, DO, PhD, PharmD, NP, PA, MS, or equivalent). Doctoral degree (MD, DO, PhD, or PharmD) preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1n71tnc&quot; data-start=&quot;4168&quot; data-end=&quot;4182&quot;&gt;Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of three years of Medical Science Liaison (MSL) experience in the pharmaceutical industry is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Rare Disease, Endocrinology, Metabolic Bone Disease, Nephrology, Rheumatology, or a related therapeutic area is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;Skills and Competencies&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to critically evaluate medical literature, interpret clinical trial data, and communicate complex scientific information clearly and accurately to healthcare professionals, investigators, and internal teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of clinical research methods and evidence generation, with the ability to stay current on disease states, treatment guidelines, standards of care, and emerging science.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to build trusted scientific relationships across a geographically dispersed territory and translate field insights into recommendations that inform Medical Affairs strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to manage field activities independently, prioritize competing demands, solve problems, and exercise sound judgment as needs change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills, including the ability to influence without authority, work effectively across functions, and lead initiatives or mentor colleagues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working knowledge of FDA regulations, Good Clinical Practice (GCP), pharmacovigilance requirements, Office of Inspector General (OIG) guidance, and applicable industry standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Medical Affairs systems and customer relationship management (CRM) platforms, and proficiency in Microsoft Office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;ewa2rj&quot; data-start=&quot;5555&quot; data-end=&quot;5580&quot;&gt;Physical Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The role requires the ability to work in a field-based environment with frequent travel, including extended periods of sitting during air, ground, and other forms of transportation. The position may require prolonged use of computers and other office equipment, as well as the ability to attend and participate in scientific meetings, conferences, advisory boards, and healthcare professional engagements. The employee must be able to navigate various work environments and maintain effective communication and presentation capabilities while traveling and performing job responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;b6ss1z&quot; data-start=&quot;5716&quot; data-end=&quot;5738&quot;&gt;Working Conditions&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Field-based position requiring up to 70% travel by air and ground transportation, including overnight travel and occasional weekend commitments to support scientific congresses, advisory boards, and other Medical Affairs activities. Must reside within the assigned territory and maintain proximity to a major airport to support regional coverage requirements, which may encompass a broad geographic area requiring regular travel. A valid driver’s license and the ability to operate a motor vehicle as required for business travel are required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kyowa Kirin reserves the right to modify this job description, at the manager’s discretion, at any time. In the US, this job description does not change your “at will” status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated base salary range for this position is $195,080 to $215,000. The actual salary offered may vary based on relevant experience, skills, qualifications, education (including applicable licenses and certifications), job-related knowledge, location, and other business and organizational needs..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The listed salary is just one component of the overall compensation package. At Kyowa Kirin North America we provide a comprehensive range of benefits including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual Bonus Program (Sales Bonus for Sales Jobs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and Holiday Schedule which includes Summer and Winter Shut-Downs, Sick Days and, Volunteer Days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare Benefits (Medical, Dental, Prescription Drugs and Vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HSA &amp;amp; FSA Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-Being and Work/Life Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life &amp;amp; Disability Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concierge Services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long Term Incentive Program (subject to job level and performance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Referral Awards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The compensation and benefits information set forth in this posting applies to candidates hired in the United States. Candidates hired outside the United States will be eligible for compensation and benefits in accordance with their local market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKNA and all of its employees have an obligation to act in accordance with the law and with integrity in all our operations and interactions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is the policy of Kyowa Kirin North America, Inc. to provide equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons without regard to race, religion, creed, color, pregnancy, sex, age, national origin, disability, genetic trait or predisposition, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation or affection preference or citizenship status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected and stored by Kyowa Kirin, Inc. (“Controller”), which is located at 510 Carnegie Center Dr. Princeton, NJ 08540 USA and can be contacted by emailing kkus.talentacquisition.8h@kyowakirin.com. Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&lt;/u&gt;. Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (“GDPR”) as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. Accordingly, if you are located outside of the United States, your personal data will be transferred to the United States once you submit it through this site. The transfer will be made using appropriate additional safeguards under the standard contractual clauses approved by regulators for transfers of personal data outside the European Union.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. &amp;nbsp;Under the GDPR, if you are located in the European Union, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability, and to lodge a complaint with an EU supervisory authority. If you have any questions about our use of your data, you may contact us by email at&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
