&lt;p&gt;Kyowa Kirin is a global specialty pharmaceutical company backed by more than 70 years of breakthrough life science innovation, dedicated to discovering and advancing treatments for diseases in which unmet need is greatest. Based in Japan with worldwide operations, we work across the continuum from drug discovery to commercialization, guided by our commitment to patients and their families.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our research teams, located in California and around the world, are focused on developing the next generation of antibody, cell, and gene therapies, with particular emphasis on bone and mineral disorders, hemato-oncology, and rare diseases. We accelerate development through collaborations with industry, academia, patients, and healthcare providers, and since 2018 we have introduced four new therapies serving patients with progressive illnesses often in need of new therapeutic alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our culture is grounded in our values:&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Commitment to Life&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Integrity&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Innovation&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;em&gt;Teamwork/Wa&lt;/em&gt;, and brought to life through the Kabegoe Principles, which define the behaviors and actions that guide how we work together to deliver meaningful impact for patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud of the progress we’ve made and mindful of the countless individuals still waiting for their own breakthroughs. A commitment to making people smile unites our efforts. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kkna.kyowakirin.com&quot;&gt;www.kkna.kyowakirin.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Global Medical/Scientific Communications leads the enterprise-wide strategy, operating model, and governance for global medical and scientific communications support for Medical Affairs, with Field Medical, congress communications, and external scientific engagement as core priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In partnership with Global Medical Strategy, Publications, Medical Education, Scientific Exchange, and regional and local Medical Affairs teams, the role translates approved strategies, scientific narratives, and evidence into clear, compelling, and compliant communications for global-to-local use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director serves as global owner of Medical/Scientific Communications content within the defined scope of the role, directs external Medical Communications agencies and partners, and establishes standards that enable consistent, scalable, and effective communications across products, disease states, and channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Senior Director operates as an individual contributor and leads through influence across a complex global matrix.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Functions:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Medical/Scientific Communications Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead enterprise-wide medical/scientific communications strategy aligned with Global Medical Affairs priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate approved product and disease-state strategies, scientific platforms, and evidence into integrated global communications plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish consistent scientific narratives, messaging frameworks, and content priorities across products, disease states, and channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate emerging evidence, external trends, and Medical Affairs needs that may influence communications priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scientific Content Development:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead development of high-quality, compliant scientific content for Medical Affairs, with Field Medical, congress communications, and external scientific exchange as core priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct external Medical Communications agencies and partners through strategic briefs and scientific direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure content is accurate, balanced, appropriately referenced, modular, scalable, and suitable for efficient global-to-local adaptation and multichannel use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scientific communication and visual standards for congress materials within scope, in partnership with Publications, Global Medical Strategy, and designated scientific owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Interfaces:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Publications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Publications and Global Medical Strategy owners to translate approved evidence and publication-derived messages into aligned downstream scientific communications, while Publications retains accountability for publication strategy and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Medical Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Global and local Medical Teams to align global scientific communications strategy, approved scientific narratives, and relevant Medical Education activities, while Medical Teams/Medical Education retains accountability for its strategy and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External Scientific Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Medical Strategy Teams, Strategic Capabilities &amp;amp; Scientific Exchange and Field Medical leadership to ensure global scientific communications strategy, narratives, and content enable high-quality, consistent, and compliant external scientific engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global-to-Local Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage global, regional and local Medical teams to incorporate relevant needs and insights into global communications planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide approved source materials, adaptation guidance, and standards that enable efficient localization while preserving local accountability for approval and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Medical Review and Content Governance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish governance for content development, review, approval, version control, distribution, maintenance, and retirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure scientific communications meet company policies and applicable legal, regulatory, privacy, and industry requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide enterprise standards and governance guidance for advisory board materials where global consistency improves efficiency; content development and execution remain locally owned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with designated medical content owners, who retain accountability for scientific accuracy and interpretation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency and Operational Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic direction and performance oversight to external Medical Communications agencies and partners, including scope, quality, budgets, timelines, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive scalable processes and systems that improve content development, approval, localization, reuse, and lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retain accountability for communications strategy, content standards, governance, and delivery decisions within the role’s defined scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration and Influence:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships across Global Medical Strategy Teams in each Therapeutic Area, regional and local Medical Affairs, Medical Information, Clinical Development, HEOR and Evidence Generation, Publications, Medical Education, Scientific Exchange, Legal, Regulatory, and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional initiatives through influence, establish clear accountabilities, resolve competing priorities, and escalate scientific, operational, or compliance risks appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Global Medical/Scientific Communications in relevant governance and cross-functional forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement and Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish outcome-focused measures for scientific quality, relevance, timeliness, adoption, reuse, stakeholder experience, and operational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use analytics, field insights, and stakeholder feedback to improve communications strategy and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance appropriate digital, automation, and AI-enabled capabilities while protecting scientific accuracy, compliance, confidentiality, and privacy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subordinates&lt;/strong&gt;: Senior individual contributor with enterprise-wide impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced degree (PhD, PharmD, MD, or equivalent) in life sciences, medicine, pharmacy, public health, biomedical sciences, or a related scientific discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional education or specialized training in medical communications, scientific communications, medical affairs, healthcare communications, or business administration is highly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 12 years of progressive experience in Medical Affairs, Medical or Scientific Communications, Field Medical, Medical Information, or related pharmaceutical or biotechnology functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum five years leading global Medical/Scientific Communications strategy, Field Medical content strategy, or comparably complex scientific communications initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate complex clinical evidence and approved scientific messages into compliant communications for Medical Affairs audiences and external scientific exchange.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in global medical review processes and global-to-local content adaptation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record directing Medical Communications agencies and partners, including strategic briefing, quality oversight, budget management, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad experience supporting multiple therapeutic areas, products, geographies, or lifecycle stages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field Medical expertise or substantial involvement in developing scientific content and resources to support Medical Science Liaison (MSL) activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of pharmaceutical industry requirements, regulatory standards, and compliance principles governing nonpromotional scientific exchange and Medical Affairs communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional scientific writing, critical appraisal, and content development skills, with the ability to translate complex clinical and scientific evidence into clear, accurate, and compelling communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in developing and deploying modular content strategies, omnichannel communications, and scalable global-to-local content approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with content management platforms, digital communications channels, content analytics, and performance measurement tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of global medical content governance frameworks, medical review processes, approval workflows, and operational best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of emerging technologies, including responsible AI applications, to enhance content development, management, and communications effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to operate independently, exercise sound judgment, manage ambiguity, and lead through influence in a global matrix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite and relevant content management, medical review, and collaboration platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise and strategic thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scientific and medical judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence without authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global and cross-cultural collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agency and stakeholder leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance and quality orientation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field and customer focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountability for results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical and scientific communications remain aligned with approved strategies, evidence, and scientific narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical Affairs teams receive timely, relevant, compliant, and usable communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Functional ownership across Global Medical Strategy, Publications, Medical Education, Scientific Exchange, and Medical/Scientific Communications remains clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global review, localization, and content lifecycle processes operate efficiently with limited avoidable rework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global content is appropriately adopted, adapted, and reused across markets and channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agency and partner deliverables meet quality, budget, and timeline expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insights, analytics, and stakeholder feedback informs communications priorities and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated salary for this position will be &lt;strong&gt;$280,000 to $315,000.&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;The actual salary offered for this role at commencement of employment may vary based on several factors including but not limited to relevant experience, skill set, qualifications, education (including applicable licenses and certifications, job-based knowledge, location, and other business and organizational needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The listed salary is just one component of the overall compensation package. At Kyowa Kirin North America we provide a comprehensive range of benefits including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual Bonus Program (Sales Bonus for Sales Jobs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and Holiday Schedule which includes Summer and Winter Shut-Downs, Sick Days and, Volunteer Days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare Benefits (Medical, Dental, Prescription Drugs and Vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HSA &amp;amp; FSA Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-Being and Work/Life Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life &amp;amp; Disability Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concierge Services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long Term Incentive Program (subject to job level and performance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Referral Awards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The compensation and benefits information set forth in this posting applies to candidates hired in the United States. Candidates hired outside the United States will be eligible for compensation and benefits in accordance with their local market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKNA and all of its employees have an obligation to act in accordance with the law and with integrity in all our operations and interactions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is the policy of Kyowa Kirin North America, Inc. to provide equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons without regard to race, religion, creed, color, pregnancy, sex, age, national origin, disability, genetic trait or predisposition, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation or affection preference or citizenship status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected and stored by Kyowa Kirin, Inc. (“Controller”), which is located at 510 Carnegie Center Dr. Princeton, NJ 08540 USA and can be contacted by emailing kkus.talentacquisition.8h@kyowakirin.com. Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at &lt;u&gt;usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&lt;/u&gt;. Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (“GDPR”) as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. Accordingly, if you are located outside of the United States, your personal data will be transferred to the United States once you submit it through this site. The transfer will be made using appropriate additional safeguards under the standard contractual clauses approved by regulators for transfers of personal data outside the European Union.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. &amp;nbsp;Under the GDPR, if you are located in the European Union, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability, and to lodge a complaint with an EU supervisory authority. If you have any questions about our use of your data, you may contact us by email at&lt;u&gt; usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;jobSectionHeader&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment &amp;amp; Staffing Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kyowa Kirin does not accept agency resumes unless contacted directly by internal Kyowa Kirin Talent Acquisition. Please do not forward resumes to Kyowa Kirin employees or any other company location; Kyowa Kirin is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-JC1&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4091935003,"name":"Global Medical Affairs","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4010013003,"name":"Princeton","location":"Princeton, New Jersey, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/kyowakirinusa90/jobs/8204724003","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6057138003,"location":{"name":"Princeton, New Jersey, United States"},"metadata":null,"id":8204724003,"updated_at":"2026-11-19T15:52:23-05:00","requisition_id":"1491","title":"Senior Director, Medical Science Liaison Head","company_name":"Kyowa Kirin North America","first_published":"2026-11-16T17:03:33-05:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Kyowa Kirin is a fast-growing global specialty pharmaceutical company that applies state-of-the-art biotechnologies to discover and deliver novel medicines in four disease areas: bone and mineral; intractable hematologic; hematology oncology; and rare disease.&amp;nbsp; A Japan-based&amp;nbsp;company, our goal is to make people smile by delivering breakthroughs where no adequate treatments currently exist, working from drug discovery to product development and commercialization. In North America, we are headquartered in Princeton, NJ, with offices in California, Massachusetts, and Ontario&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Senior Director, Kyowa Kirin North America (KKNA) Medical Science Liaison Head provides strategic and operational leadership for Medical Science Liaison teams across KKNA therapeutic areas. This role establishes the enterprise MSL vision, operating model, and annual and long-range strategic plans; drives consistent, high-quality field execution; and develops field medical leadership capabilities. The Senior Director ensures that scientific exchange, external stakeholder engagement, and medical insights advance Medical Affairs and organizational priorities while meeting the highest standards of scientific integrity, ethics, and compliance. The role serves as a senior Medical Affairs leader and strategic partner, ensuring that field medical perspectives inform evidence generation, launch readiness, lifecycle planning, and organizational decision-making. Through a dotted-line relationship with the Global Head of Medical Strategic Capabilities and Scientific Exchange, the role ensures alignment of KKNA MSL strategy and execution with the Global Field Medical operating model and standards, while addressing regional needs and applicable local requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;1222&quot; data-end=&quot;1225&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1peydm1&quot; data-start=&quot;1227&quot; data-end=&quot;1250&quot;&gt;Essential Functions&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership and Organizational Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead, coach, and develop MSL Directors, Associate Directors, and MSLs across therapeutic areas, establishing clear accountabilities, leadership expectations, succession plans, and talent-development priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and sustain a high-performing, inclusive, and collaborative field medical organization capable of operating effectively across therapeutic areas and within a complex matrix environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish a performance-management framework that aligns team objectives, field execution standards, and outcomes with Medical Affairs priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Regularly evaluate organizational and individual performance, provide timely feedback, and implement development or improvement plans as appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define the MSL capability framework and proficiency expectations; identify organizational capability gaps; and oversee development plans that strengthen scientific expertise, insight generation, stakeholder engagement, and communication effectiveness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure MSL teams remain current on product data, clinical evidence, scientific literature, industry developments, and regulations governing field medical activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead organizational change and the adoption of new capabilities, technologies, processes, and ways of working that enhance field medical effectiveness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Planning and Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the development, prioritization, and execution of annual and long-range MSL strategies, operating plans, and budgets in alignment with therapeutic area, Medical Affairs, and enterprise objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish thought leader and healthcare professional engagement strategies that support meaningful scientific exchange and address defined medical and patient needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate organizational priorities into clear field medical objectives, execution standards, resource plans, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Allocate people, budget, and technology resources based on strategic priorities, scientific opportunity, patient need, and anticipated field medical impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify emerging opportunities and risks and recommend adjustments to strategy, operating plans, and resource deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scientific Exchange, Stakeholder Engagement, and Medical Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide leadership to MSL teams in building trusted scientific relationships with thought leaders, healthcare professionals, academic institutions, and other relevant external stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure that external scientific exchange is evidence-based, balanced, responsive to stakeholder needs, and conducted in accordance with applicable policies and standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish expectations and processes for the systematic collection, synthesis, escalation, communication, and application of field medical insights to ensure these inform evidence-generation plans, medical strategy, educational priorities, launch readiness, lifecycle planning, and organizational decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evaluate the quality and strategic relevance of stakeholder engagement and medical insights, not solely the volume of activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent the MSL function in senior internal and external forums, as appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional and Enterprise Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the senior MSL function partner to Medical Directors, Global Medical Affairs, Clinical Development, Research, Franchise, Commercial, Market Access, and other relevant leadership teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clarify roles, decision rights, and ways of working between MSL teams and cross-functional partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide senior leadership with clear recommendations regarding field medical priorities, capabilities, organizational design, resource requirements, risks, and opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Champion the strategic value of the MSL organization and communicate its contribution to Medical Affairs and enterprise objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance, Impact, and Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the MSL performance and impact framework, including the selection, implementation, monitoring, and communication of quantitative and qualitative measures that demonstrate execution quality, stakeholder value, insight impact, and progress against strategic objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use data, analytics, and field intelligence to guide resource allocation, identify performance trends, and improve MSL effectiveness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide senior leadership with timely, balanced assessments of risks, resource needs, and opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sponsor continuous improvement initiatives that strengthen MSL processes, systems, governance, and stakeholder experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance, Ethics, and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set and model high standards and ensure that MSL activities adhere to applicable laws, regulations, policies, standard operating procedures, and Medical Affairs governance requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure teams receive appropriate training and understand their individual accountability for compliant execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify, escalate, and address compliance, quality, operational, or reputational risks associated with field medical activities and partner with Legal, Regulatory, Compliance, and other control functions to strengthen governance and resolve identified gaps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2433&quot; data-end=&quot;2547&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr data-start=&quot;4051&quot; data-end=&quot;4054&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;g9ewcs&quot; data-start=&quot;4056&quot; data-end=&quot;4069&quot;&gt;Education&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;A doctoral level scientific or clinical degree, such as MD, PharmD, or PhD, is preferred. A relevant advanced degree or professional qualification in the life sciences, nursing, pharmacy, medicine, or a related discipline is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1n71tnc&quot; data-start=&quot;4168&quot; data-end=&quot;4182&quot;&gt;Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 []&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A minimum of 10 years of progressive experience in Medical Affairs or field medical leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least five years of experience leading managers and geographically dispersed medical teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated success developing and executing field medical strategy across multiple therapeutic areas, products, or lifecycle stages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing budgets, organizational resources, operating plans, and competing strategic priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven ability to partner with senior cross-functional and global leaders in a complex matrix organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated experience leading organizational change, capability development, and continuous-improvement initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience supporting launch readiness, evidence generation, medical insights, and lifecycle planning is strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior field medical or MSL experience is preferred&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated enterprise leadership, strategic thinking, and sound judgment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to translate organizational priorities into clear objectives, operating plans, execution standards, and resource decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven success leading leaders, building high-performing teams, developing talent, and strengthening succession pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to guide teams through ambiguity, complexity, growth, and organizational change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exceptional executive communication, influencing, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to build alignment across a complex multinational matrix while maintaining scientific integrity and appropriate Medical Affairs independence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong business and financial acumen, with disciplined execution and accountability for outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify organizational risks and opportunities and present clear, evidence-based recommendations to senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cultural sensitivity and the ability to establish trust and consensus across diverse teams and stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong commitment to patient needs, scientific excellence, continuous learning, and talent development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment while managing ambiguity effectively. Commitment to the highest ethical, legal, regulatory, and scientific standards. Demonstrated professionalism, sound judgment, and scientific integrity. Passion for personal learning and professional development. Cultural sensitivity and adaptability within multinational organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Normal office or remote-working environment with prolonged sitting and extensive computer work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to drive or fly to meetings and business activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position requires up to 50% of domestic and international travel, including occasional weekend commitments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The anticipated base salary range for this position is &lt;strong&gt;$290,000 to $325,000&lt;/strong&gt;. The actual base salary offered may vary based on relevant experience, skills, qualifications, education, applicable licenses and certifications, job-related knowledge, location, and business and organizational needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary is one part of the total compensation package. Kyowa Kirin North America offers:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;401(k) with company match&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Annual bonus program&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Paid time off and holidays, including summer and winter shutdowns, sick days, and volunteer days&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Medical, dental, prescription drug, and vision coverage&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Health savings account (HSA) and flexible spending account (FSA) programs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Well-being and work-life programs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Life and disability insurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Concierge services&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Long-term incentive program, subject to job level and performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pet insurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employee referral awards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The compensation and benefits described in this posting apply to candidates hired in the United States. Candidates hired outside the United States are eligible for compensation and benefits in accordance with their local market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrity and Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKNA and all of its employees have an obligation to act in accordance with the law and with integrity in all our operations and interactions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is the policy of Kyowa Kirin North America, Inc. to provide equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons without regard to race, religion, creed, color, pregnancy, sex, age, national origin, disability, genetic trait or predisposition, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation or affection preference or citizenship status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected and stored by Kyowa Kirin, Inc. (“Controller”), which is located at 510 Carnegie Center Dr. Princeton, NJ 08540 USA and can be contacted by emailing &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:kkus.talentacquisition.8h@kyowakirin.com&quot;&gt;kkus.talentacquisition.8h@kyowakirin.com&lt;/a&gt;. Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&quot;&gt;usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (“GDPR”) as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. Accordingly, if you are located outside of the United States, your personal data will be transferred to the United States once you submit it through this site. The transfer will be made using appropriate additional safeguards under the standard contractual clauses approved by regulators for transfers of personal data outside the European Union.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. Under the GDPR, if you are located in the European Union, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability, and to lodge a complaint with an EU supervisory authority. If you have any questions about our use of your data, you may contact us by email at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&quot;&gt;usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment &amp;amp; Staffing Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kyowa Kirin accepts agency resumes only when its internal Talent Acquisition team contacts the agency directly. Please do not forward unsolicited resumes to Kyowa Kirin employees or company locations. Kyowa Kirin is not responsible for fees associated with unsolicited resumes.&lt;/p&gt;
