&lt;h2&gt;About Kyowa Kirin&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kyowa Kirin is a fast-growing global specialty pharmaceutical company that applies state-of-the-art biotechnology to discover and deliver novel medicines in four areas: bone and mineral disorders, intractable hematologic disorders, hematologic oncology, and rare disease. Based in Japan, we aim to make people smile by delivering breakthroughs where adequate treatments do not exist. Our work spans drug discovery, product development, and commercialization. Our North American headquarters is in Princeton, New Jersey, with offices in California, Massachusetts, and Ontario.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Job Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Medical Science Liaison (MSL), Oncology is a field-based member of Kyowa Kirin’s Medical Affairs team and serves as a scientific and clinical expert for the assigned therapeutic area and products. The Senior MSL builds trusted relationships with healthcare professionals, key opinion leaders, researchers, and other external stakeholders to facilitate accurate, balanced, and evidence-based scientific exchange.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior MSL brings field insights to Medical Affairs to inform medical strategy, evidence generation, and cross-functional decision-making. The role operates in accordance with applicable regulations, industry standards, and company policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain scientific relationships with national, regional, and local key opinion leaders, healthcare professionals, clinical investigators, and other external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage in compliant, peer-to-peer scientific exchange on Kyowa Kirin products, disease states, and emerging clinical data. Respond to unsolicited requests for medical information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and communicate actionable medical insights, unmet medical needs, and competitive intelligence to inform Medical Affairs strategy and evidence generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the regional scientific expert and connect external stakeholders with appropriate Medical Affairs resources, initiatives, and opportunities for scientific collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support scientific engagement at medical congresses, advisory boards, investigator meetings, and other scientific forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with clinical investigators and partner with Clinical Operations to support investigator-initiated studies and company-sponsored clinical research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver scientific presentations, educational programs, and clinical resources for healthcare professionals and other appropriate stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide scientific training to internal partners on disease states, treatment landscapes, clinical data, and Kyowa Kirin products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Medical Affairs, Clinical Development, Commercial, Market Access, and Regulatory Affairs while maintaining appropriate boundaries between scientific and commercial activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate product safety information in accordance with company procedures, pharmacovigilance requirements, and applicable regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on clinical literature, treatment guidelines, and emerging data in the assigned therapeutic area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Medical Affairs initiatives and strategic planning. Mentor fellow MSLs by sharing scientific expertise, field insights, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Job Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An advanced clinical or scientific degree or healthcare professional credential is required, such as an MD, DO, PhD, PharmD, NP, PA, MS, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A doctoral degree (MD, DO, PhD, or PharmD) is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Three or more years of experience as an MSL, field-based medical professional, or in a related clinical, scientific, or Medical Affairs role is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in oncology or a related disease state is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to engage healthcare professionals, key opinion leaders, and clinical investigators through compliant scientific exchange.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret clinical and scientific data and communicate it effectively to different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with investigator-initiated studies or company-sponsored clinical trials is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scientific congresses, advisory boards, investigator meetings, or other medical education activities is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage field responsibilities, prioritize activities, and work independently in alignment with Medical Affairs objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of relevant disease states, treatment guidelines, and current standards of care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with clinical research methods, evidence generation, and interpretation of clinical trial data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of FDA regulations, Good Clinical Practice, pharmacovigilance requirements, Office of Inspector General guidance, and applicable industry standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to evaluate medical literature, synthesize complex data, identify trends in field insights, and deliver accurate, balanced scientific presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Medical Affairs systems and customer relationship management platforms, along with proficiency in Microsoft Office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written, verbal, listening, and presentation skills, with the ability to build working relationships and manage conflict effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment, scientific integrity, and the ability to manage competing priorities and adapt in a fast-paced, multinational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to ongoing professional development and high ethical, legal, regulatory, and scientific standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Travel and Work Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This field-based role requires up to 70% travel by air and ground, including overnight travel and occasional weekends for scientific congresses, advisory boards, and other Medical Affairs activities. A valid driver’s license and the ability to drive for business travel are required. The role may involve extended periods of sitting during travel and prolonged computer use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated base salary range for this position is &lt;strong&gt;$195,080 to $215,000&lt;/strong&gt;. The actual base salary offered may vary based on relevant experience, skills, qualifications, education, applicable licenses and certifications, job-related knowledge, location, and business and organizational needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary is one part of the total compensation package. Kyowa Kirin North America offers the following benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual bonus program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid time off and holidays, including summer and winter shutdowns, sick days, and volunteer days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, prescription drug, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health savings account (HSA) and flexible spending account (FSA) programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-being and work-life programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life and disability insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concierge services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long-term incentive program, subject to job level and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee referral awards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The compensation and benefits described in this posting apply to candidates hired in the United States. Candidates hired outside the United States are eligible for compensation and benefits in accordance with their local market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Integrity and Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKNA and all of its employees have an obligation to act in accordance with the law and with integrity in all our operations and interactions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is the policy of Kyowa Kirin North America, Inc. to provide equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons without regard to race, religion, creed, color, pregnancy, sex, age, national origin, disability, genetic trait or predisposition, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation or affection preference or citizenship status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected and stored by Kyowa Kirin, Inc. (“Controller”), which is located at 510 Carnegie Center Dr. Princeton, NJ 08540 USA and can be contacted by emailing &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:kkus.talentacquisition.8h@kyowakirin.com&quot;&gt;kkus.talentacquisition.8h@kyowakirin.com&lt;/a&gt;. Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&quot;&gt;usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (“GDPR”) as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. Accordingly, if you are located outside of the United States, your personal data will be transferred to the United States once you submit it through this site. The transfer will be made using appropriate additional safeguards under the standard contractual clauses approved by regulators for transfers of personal data outside the European Union.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. Under the GDPR, if you are located in the European Union, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability, and to lodge a complaint with an EU supervisory authority. If you have any questions about our use of your data, you may contact us by email at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&quot;&gt;usprivacyoffice@kyowakirin.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Recruitment &amp;amp; Staffing Agencies&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kyowa Kirin accepts agency resumes only when its internal Talent Acquisition team contacts the agency directly. Please do not forward unsolicited resumes to Kyowa Kirin employees or company locations. Kyowa Kirin is not responsible for fees associated with unsolicited resumes.&lt;/p&gt;
